{comment: Intro}
[|][F]            [|][F]            [|][Bb2]          [|][Bb2]          [|]

{comment: Verse 1}
Early in the morning [F]boats are in the harbor
[F]Ropes along the water [Bb2]waiting for the tide to turn
Early in the morning [Dm7]gulls are on the railing
[C(4)]Calling from the old stone [Bb2]pier
Early in the evening [F]lights are on the water
[F]Windows on the hillside [Bb2]glowing as the boats come in
Early in the evening [Dm7]nets are on the dock
[C(4)]Folded for the morning [Bb2]waiting till we sail again
[N.C.] We’ll sail out from here

{comment: Chorus}
[F]Row now row now row to the harbor
[Bb2]Row now row now row to the harbor
[Dm7]Home is [C(4)]calling
Yes [Bb2]home is calling all of the [F]boats

{comment: Verse 2}
Early in the winter [F]ice is on the water
[F]Snow along the shoreline [Bb2]drifting ‘til the morning sun
Early in the winter [Dm7]fires in the harbor
[C(4)]Warm against the cold sea [Bb2]wind
[N.C.] We’ll sail out from here

{comment: Instrumental}
[|][F]            [|][C/F]          [|][F]            [|][Dm/F]         [|]

{comment: Bridge}
[Dm7]Every boat comes in [C(4)]every sail is thin
[F/A]Every rope is wound  [Bb2] we’ll sail out from here
[Dm7]Every light is low [C(4)]every road is home
[F/A]Every bell has rung  [Bb2] we’ll sail out from here

